    <briefdescription>
<para>Creates a triangular element mesh from the pixels of the regular grid. Boundaries that are defined by changes in the pixel values are used to control how the pixels are split such that a smooth boundary is created. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Stephan K. Matthai </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="author"><para>Stephen G. Roberts </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>1999</para>
</simplesect>
</para>
<sect1 id="compare_floats_8h_1motivation">
<title>Motivation</title><para>Have a simple procedure to go from a geometry drawn with a pixel-type tool or defined by a processed image, to go to a simple triangular finite-element mesh for CSP computations. </para>
</sect1>
